# Environnement de developpement
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Sorties de test hors tests/golden (qui, lui, est versionne)
/tmp/

# Resolution lock written by `uv run` and `uv lock`. Not committed, because
# nothing reads it: CI installs with `uv pip install -e ".[dev]"`, which ignores
# the file, and switching to `uv sync` would uninstall the validators installed
# alongside it (ansible-core, ansible-lint, yamllint). A lock nobody consumes
# buys no reproducibility.
#
# Leaving it untracked, on the other hand, was expensive: the first `uv run` of
# the workflow dirtied CI's own checkout, and
# `tests/conftest.py::template_is_dirty` then skipped the only test of
# `forge update` -- every run, on all three Python versions, unnoticed.
uv.lock
